# Retire policy 2026-11-20: production ended 2013; retire dates are road-presence estimates, staggered by colourway.
# Nissan Qashqai, first generation (J10), 2006-2013.
#
# The five objects keep their original names (rule 9, savegame
# validity). The graphics were replaced on 2026-11-17 with a J10 model built
# from photographs, so the shell now represents the first-generation car rather
# than a generic crossover. The J11 and J12 are separate objects.
#
# Dimensions 4.315 x 1.780 x 1.605 m, wheelbase 2.630 m, from the English
# Wikipedia J10 dimension box. Metres master: citycars/4.5/nissan-qashqai-j10.blend.
# Interchange: citycars/4.5/nissan-qashqai-j10.dae (49 objects). References:
# citycars/references/nissan-qashqai-j10/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the body and lamps remain visibly low-poly, and the
# crossover's rising waist is simplified. At 128 px the tall body, the high
# beltline and the hatch slope read correctly.
#
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nissan_Qashqai
obj=citycar
name=NissanQashqai(Blue)
copyright=James/JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=6
intro_year=2006
intro_month=8
retire_year=2021
retire_month=6
speed=135
class=1
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=125
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=518

